{"discussion":"The public check reveals two issues: (1) `_is_union` only checks `types.UnionType` (PEP 604 `|` form) but doesn't detect `typing.Union[int, str]` which in this environment is NOT a `types.UnionType` instance. (2) A syntax error in the test file: `typing.Union[list[int], int)` has `)` where `]` is needed. Fix `_is_union` to also detect `typing.Union` via `__origin__`.","account":"Task: Add union registration to singledispatch. PEP 604 (|) form works; typing.Union form fails because _is_union only checks types.UnionType. Fix: extend _is_union to also check __origin__ is typing.Union. Also fix syntax error in test file line 74: 'int)' should be 'int]' to close Union subscript. Candidate: ae2d86b9. Two patches needed.","operation":{"action":"patch","path":"Lib/functools.py","old":"def _is_union(cls):
    return isinstance(cls, types.UnionType)","new":"def _is_union(cls):
    if isinstance(cls, types.UnionType):
        return True
    import typing
    return getattr(cls, '__origin__', None) is typing.Union","expected_candidate_id":"ae2d86b9034b2a4867603de8a1ca1795e3640ce7e67736a72873cf2b77d4d8e9","expected_file_sha256":"aedbd289b685af3ac3b59a766942e686fae922856ca0755d3eb11b9bea850521"}}
